  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 129 PM MDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nUpper high center finally shifts into the srn Plains on Wed, \nthen moves even farther east starting Thursday, ending up \nsomewhere over the sern U.S. by the weekend. Resulting upper \npattern continues to look favorable for an influx of moisture \nand widespread showers and thunderstorms starting Wed and \npersisting into the weekend across the entire region. Rainfall \ncould be enhanced at times by weak upper level disturbances \nlifting over the wrn periphery of the ridge, with at least a \ncouple weak cold fronts and associated ely upslope surges \nproviding increased low level moisture over the ern mountains \nand plains. Heavy rainfall and flash flooding from slow-moivng\nstorms continues to look like a threat from Wed onward,\nespecially over recent burn scars, and even unburned locations \nand urban areas may see increased potential for flooding with\nrepeated rounds of heavy rainfall. As the high moves away, mid\nlevel temps cool, and with added help from clouds and precip,\nmax temps may actually end up a little lower than seasonal\naverages for a change, especially Fri/Sat.",
